## Fix: final whole-branch review (microbatch freshness, settings, sync schedule, scheduled MV refresh)
================================================================================

Context: The final whole-branch review found four Important issues: a
`microbatch` `_data` view never refreshed between builds; the
`serverless_pipelines_enabled` / `slot_pipeline_channel` settings were never
declared (always on / PREVIEW); a runtime incremental failure re-registered the
Lakebase synced table as a snapshot; and a scheduled tick replaced the
incremental `_data` view by a CTAS (before even probing). It also listed minors:
an empty graph after a net-apply fallback recorded a base, unused code, copies to
share, row-local relationship mappings that lose rows, and two doc gaps.

Changes:

1. src/back/core/graphdb/delta/MaterializedViewBuilder.py,
   src/back/core/streaming/SlotPipelineSpec.py,
   src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/TwinIncrementalBuild.py
   A `microbatch` `_data` MV gets `TRIGGER ON UPDATE` when it reads at most ten
   relations (`SlotPipelineSpec.mv_source_count`: `_slots` plus table-based batch
   mappings; unknown with a `sql_query` or a join), else
   `SCHEDULE CRON '0 0/15 * * * ?' AT TIME ZONE 'UTC'`. Verified against the
   CREATE MATERIALIZED VIEW reference
   (https://docs.databricks.com/aws/en/sql/language-manual/sql-ref-syntax-ddl-create-materialized-view):
   `SCHEDULE EVERY` only takes hours, days or weeks, so the requested
   "SCHEDULE EVERY 15 MINUTES" is not valid and a Quartz cron is used; an unset
   session time zone is an error, so the zone is given; TRIGGER ON UPDATE allows
   at most ten upstream sources. The clause is part of the definition
   fingerprint (unchanged without a clause); `incremental` and the MERGE table
   get none; the chosen clause is logged, the trace keys are unchanged.
2. src/shared/config/settings.py, docs/getting-started.md
   `serverless_pipelines_enabled` (ONTOBRICKS_SERVERLESS_PIPELINES_ENABLED,
   default true) and `slot_pipeline_channel` (ONTOBRICKS_SLOT_PIPELINE_CHANNEL,
   PREVIEW or CURRENT, anything else refused) are declared and documented.
3. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/TwinMergeFallback.py,
   src/back/objects/registry/schedule/build.py
   `TwinMergeFallback.promotes(decision, detail)` is the MERGE-promotion
   predicate; the scheduled tick (`_tick_modes`) uses it, so with serverless off
   an incremental domain syncs TRIGGERED on a tick like its MERGE main build.
4. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/TwinLakebaseSync.py,
   src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/TwinIncrementalBuild.py,
   src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/_build_pipeline.py
   The sync schedule follows `sync_schedule_mode`, the resolver's decision before
   any runtime fallback (`_fall_back` does not touch it; a MERGE promotion sets
   `incremental`), so a transient failure keeps a triggered/continuous
   registration; `materialization_mode_effective` still traces `full`.
5. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/TwinScheduledRefresh.py (new,
   re-exported), src/back/objects/registry/schedule/build.py
   A tick decides (and probes) before writing; an existing incremental `_data`
   MV is refreshed in place (`incremental`: one triggered slot-pipeline update
   via `TwinIncrementalBuild.run_update`, then REFRESH; `microbatch`: REFRESH
   only); `full`, MERGE-promoted domains, a non-MV `_data` or a missing slot
   pipeline keep the CTAS.
6. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/_build_pipeline.py
   The empty-graph completion clears `apply_mode`, `data_table_version` and
   `data_table_id` (the store was not touched, so the run is no base).
7. Dead code removed: `SourceReadiness.source_overwritten_since` / `enable_sql`
   (docs quote the ALTER TABLE instead), `MaterializedViewBuilder.explain_sql` /
   `plan_is_incremental` and their regexes / `_texts`,
   `SlotPipelineRunner.read_event_log_technique`, `slots_complete`, and the
   `_BuildPipeline._count_view_triples` alias (one compute-once test that called
   it removed); a stale `_report_post_sync_triple_count` docstring fixed.
8. Duplication: `TwinIncrementalBuild.compile_for` serves the main build, the
   MERGE fingerprint and the tick; the slot pipeline name takes its version from
   `TwinBuildRunHistory.build_run_key`; `materialize.relation_exists(...,
   strict=True)` replaces `TwinSlotReconciliation.slots_table_listed`.
9. src/back/core/streaming/SlotProjectionCompiler.py
   Relationship mappings always classify as batch (several objects of one
   subject would collapse onto one slot); docs say row-local entity mappings need
   a unique id column.
10. docs/incremental-materialization.md, src/front/templates/settings.html
    Modes table and known limitations describe the microbatch refresh; the
    Continuous option names the continuous slot pipeline and the view refresh;
    the MERGE skip does not reset `_inferred`; `/dtwin/databricks-build/start`
    CTAS-es over the MV and never stops a microbatch pipeline (known limitation);
    the scheduled-build and sync-schedule behaviour is described.
11. Tests: tests/units/graphdb/delta/test_materialized_view_builder.py,
    tests/units/graphdb/delta/test_delta_package.py,
    tests/units/streaming/test_slot_projection_compiler.py,
    tests/units/streaming/test_source_readiness.py,
    tests/units/streaming/test_slot_pipeline_runner.py,
    tests/units/objects/test_build_pipeline_modes.py,
    tests/units/objects/test_build_pipeline_net_apply.py,
    tests/units/objects/test_build_pipeline_compute_once.py (one test removed:
    it called the removed alias), tests/units/registry/test_scheduled_build_lakeflow_source.py,
    tests/units/settings/test_config.py,
    tests/units/front/test_settings_lakebase_sync_defaults.py.

