## Fix: final review residuals (sync schedule on a failed probe or MERGE; stale view on a tick)
================================================================================

Context: The re-review of the final fix wave confirmed the microbatch clause,
the settings and the scheduled refresh, and found two remaining issues. The main
build still re-registered a triggered synced table as a snapshot when the
row-tracking probe raised (before the schedule was set) or when the MERGE failed
(the schedule stayed full before the CTAS), while a scheduled tick left the
registration alone or kept TRIGGERED. And a scheduled tick refreshed any
materialized view of ours in place, so mappings edited since the last main build
were regenerated into the gateway VIEW while `_data` silently kept the old
definition.

Changes:

1. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/TwinBuildPostMaterialize.py,
   src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/TwinIncrementalBuild.py,
   src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/TwinMergeFallback.py
   New `TwinBuildPostMaterialize.gate_decision` (the resolver with the sources
   counted as tracked; `decide_mode_for` uses it for its probe gate). The sync
   schedule starts from it before the probe and is refined after the probe;
   `TwinMergeFallback.apply` sets `incremental` as soon as it runs, so a failed
   MERGE (CTAS) keeps it. `materialization_mode_effective` still reports the
   mode that ran. By hand: a tick whose probe fails raises in `_tick_modes`
   before `ensure` (registration untouched); a tick with serverless off resolves
   (data_mode, sync_mode) = (full, incremental), i.e. TRIGGERED, like the main
   build's MERGE.
2. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/TwinScheduledRefresh.py,
   src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/TwinIncrementalBuild.py,
   src/back/objects/registry/schedule/build.py
   The tick hands its mappings down; `TwinScheduledRefresh.refresh` recompiles
   them, compares the MV definition fingerprint
   (`TwinIncrementalBuild.data_definition_for`, now shared with the main build,
   refresh clause included) and the slot pipeline's stored SQL fingerprint, and
   on any mismatch (or unknown mappings) logs why and leaves `_data` to the CTAS.
3. docs/incremental-materialization.md, src/front/templates/settings.html,
   changelogs/v0.9.1/dermot-smyth_2026-11-02.log
   Reconcile answers 502; the wrong live-unverified bullet about TRIGGER ON
   UPDATE upstreams is removed (here and from the final-review section); the
   spike checklist gains three items; a follow-up line names the unreachable
   relationship branches (left in place: deleting them with their tests is
   ~85 lines); the Continuous option mentions the 15-minute schedule.
4. tests/units/objects/test_build_pipeline_compute_once.py
   The vacuous `_count_view_triples` and `slots_complete` assignments removed.
5. Tests: tests/units/objects/test_build_pipeline_modes.py (failed probe keeps
   TRIGGERED; a gated domain schedules a snapshot),
   tests/units/objects/test_build_pipeline_net_apply.py (failed MERGE keeps
   TRIGGERED), tests/units/registry/test_scheduled_build_lakeflow_source.py
   (unchanged definition refreshes in place; changed batch mapping or slot SQL,
   unknown mappings -> CTAS; the change is logged),
   tests/units/front/test_settings_lakebase_sync_defaults.py.

