## Design traceability: closing the Phase 1/2 gaps
================================================================================

Context: The design review traced seven Phase 1/2 commitments that the branch did
not yet keep: a source rewrite (INSERT OVERWRITE, CREATE OR REPLACE, TRUNCATE,
RESTORE) silently broke the slot pipeline's change feed; nothing told an operator,
before a build, why a domain would run as `full` or let them fix it; the
"EXPLAIN says incremental" check had been deleted as unused; there was no
incremental status view; reconciliation compared only `_slots` with `_data` and
never ran unattended; Neo4j net apply; and no property test of the slot fold. The
re-review of the follow-up round added one Important finding (the MERGE added
`object_hash` without backfilling it) and two stale notes.

Changes:

1. src/back/core/streaming/SourceReadiness.py, src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/
   TwinIncrementalBuild.py, TwinSlotPipeline.py, TwinBuildRunHistory.py,
   _build_pipeline.py (efc08a5d)
   Source overwrite detection: every build records `source_versions` (latest Delta
   version per slot-pipeline source) in `stats.materialization`; the next build
   reads `DESCRIBE HISTORY` of each source since the base run's version
