## Fix: design-gaps re-review
================================================================================

Context: The re-review confirmed the five Important findings and the minors of
the previous round, and found one new Important finding (NULL-subject rows made
reconciliation drift forever), three minors (a transient history failure dropped
the tick's view for a CTAS, the bounded history read could miss a version, an
empty facts dict was traced), the nightly EXPLAIN step still non-blocking, and a
missing upgrade note.

Changes:

1. src/back/core/streaming/SlotReconciler.py (b41b5e18)
   N1: the gateway VIEW (and a batch branch) keeps the NULL-subject triple a NULL
   source key produces, the slot view drops the row; every reconciliation then
   showed `view_data` drift and the drift's full refresh never cleared it. The
   reconciler counts and hashes only rows with a subject and a non-blank object
   (`_RECONCILED_TRIPLES`, reconciler only; the MV and VIEW SQL are unchanged).
   Regression test: a VIEW with one NULL-subject row and matching slots is no drift
   (SQLite-backed). The synced table, whose key cannot hold a NULL subject, is still
   compared with those rows.
2. src/back/core/streaming/SourceReadiness.py (7cc29e37)
   N3: the bounded `DESCRIBE HISTORY` reads one row more (`LIMIT versions since + 1`,
   so a commit landing between the version read and the history read stays covered);
   a history whose oldest returned version is above `since + 1` (log retention) or
   that is empty counts as a rewrite.
3. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/TwinScheduledRefresh.py,
   src/back/objects/registry/schedule/build.py (71c95af7)
   N2: a source history the tick cannot read leaves `_data` as it is for that tick
   (nothing refreshed, dropped or recorded; warning) instead of a CTAS every later
   tick would repeat until a manual build. N4: a tick that fails before any fact was
   recorded no longer traces an empty `materialization` dict (`_trace_stats`).
4. .github/workflows/nightly.yml, docs/incremental-materialization.md (52c91680)
   The external smoke probe stays non-blocking without the EXPLAIN test; the
   EXPLAIN check is its own step (run when the integration secrets are set) that
   writes a step summary, annotates a failure and fails the job, so the nightly
   regression issue is opened. The integration credentials move to the job env.
   Docs: the blocking step, the NULL-subject exclusion, the history coverage rule,
   the tick's unreadable-history rule, and an upgrade note — after upgrading, run
   one build per `incremental` / `microbatch` domain (the slot SQL fingerprint
   changed with the delete rank: that build does one full refresh, ticks CTAS
   `_data` until then).

Known limitations (follow-ups):
- If Lakeflow syncs NULL-subject rows of `_data` (it should refuse a NULL key),
  `sync_data` would differ by those rows; live-unverified.
- The conservative history rules (more than 10000 versions; a history cut by log
  retention) force a full refresh rather than risk a missed rewrite.

