## Fix: Phase 3 core review
================================================================================

Context: Review of the Phase 3 processing core (Implementer B): one Critical
finding (state evicted by the TTL lost tombstones), three Important ones
(key-changing updates, Spark string rendering, a wrong "pure Python" claim) and
minors.

Changes:

1. src/back/core/streaming/SlotDiffProcessor.py (Critical)
   A key with no state, never seen or evicted by the MapState TTL, is unknown:
   any slot of it may still be live in `_live`. Its first event upserts every
   non-blank slot and tombstones every other predicate the mapping can produce
   (a delete tombstones them all); the sink's seq guard absorbs the extra
   tombstones. Before, a delete after an eviction emitted nothing and the
   `_live` row stayed `deleted = false`. The docstring states that the TTL
   must exceed the maximum event lateness and that without a TTL the state
   keeps a watermark per predicate of every key it saw (unbounded growth).
2. src/back/core/streaming/SlotRowProjector.py (Important, minor)
   `spark_string(value, column)` accepts strings, integers, booleans and
   `None` only and raises `ValidationError` naming the column otherwise:
   Python renders floats, decimals, dates and nested values unlike Spark's
   `CAST(... AS STRING)`, so the stream casts every source column to STRING
   in Spark before serialising the row. Columns are looked up
   case-insensitively, as Spark resolves them; `project(row)` returns the key,
   subject and slots from one lower-cased copy; `predicates()` is a method
   (`rdf:type`, `rdfs:label` when there is a label column, the attributes).
3. src/jobs/triple_stream/processor.py (Important, minors)
   The module docstring no longer claims the logic is pure Python: importing
   it loads the application package, so the job needs OntoBricks installed on
   the cluster; it also states the string-valued row and TTL contracts. The
   unused logger and the `noqa` noise are removed; `_store`'s docstring says
   that an applied event rewrites every entry (each carries the event's seq).
4. src/back/core/streaming/__init__.py
   Imports sorted (ruff I001).
5. Tests: tests/property/test_slot_diff_property.py rebuilt on a generic
   model: three mappings on one table (one with the composite key
   `region|num`), key-changing updates whose input rows delete the old key
   (Important 2), NULL keys through the processor path, tab objects (not
   blank, as `TRIM` strips spaces only), in-order, out-of-order and replayed
   delivery, TTL evictions and a start from a `_slots` snapshot; its AUTO CDC
   model is checked against `test_slot_fold.py`'s, and the SQL oracle in
   tests/units/streaming/test_slot_row_projector.py no longer uses
   `spark_string` (string rows only). Unit tests: evicted state + delete,
   evicted state + blank column, unknown mapping delete, tab objects, strict
   casts, case-insensitive lookups (test_slot_diff_processor.py,
   test_slot_row_projector.py, tests/units/jobs/test_triple_stream_processor.py).

