## Phase 3 (realtime): resolver, Lakebase _live, RTM job, DAB pipelines, orchestration
================================================================================

Context: The deferred `realtime` mode is now built as far as it can be without a
live workspace (Implementer A; the pure processor classes are Implementer B's
section above): the resolver honours a per-domain topic, Lakebase serves a `_live`
table through the union view, a Real-Time-Mode job streams the topic into it, the
app starts / stops / reports the stream, the reconciliation compares `_live` with
the slots, and the per-(domain, version) slot pipelines become DAB-deployable (the
Phase 1 "deployed via DAB" gap).

Changes:

1. src/back/core/graphdb/RealtimeSource.py (new, re-exported),
   MaterializationModeResolver.py, GraphDBFactory.py, src/shared/config/settings.py,
   TwinBuildPostMaterialize.py, TwinIncrementalReadiness.py, Domain.py,
   DomainSession.py, the domain template / JS, navbar.js (48edb138, 07e9a1e2)
   A domain's `realtime_source` ({kind kafka|eventhubs|kinesis, bootstrap_servers,
   topic, secret_scope, secret_key, key_format json}; names only — any other field
   such as a password is refused) is validated, persisted and round-tripped; with
   `ONTOBRICKS_REALTIME_ENABLED` on and a Lakebase backend it makes
   `realtime_topic_available`, which the resolver now honours (realtime runs
   realtime on the microbatch pipeline; serverless, the backend and row tracking
   gate it like microbatch; else `realtime_not_available` as before). An effective
   realtime builds like microbatch (`CONTINUOUS_MATERIALIZATION_MODES`: continuous
   slot pipeline, self-refreshing view, continuous sync, tick view refresh). The
   readiness preflight reports `realtime` facts; the domain panel enables the
   option and shows the source fields. New settings: realtime_enabled,
   realtime_job_name, realtime_lakebase_user / _secret, realtime_checkpoint_root.
2. src/back/core/graphdb/lakebase/_companion_ddl.py, LakebaseLiveTable.py (new,
