Known limitations (follow-ups):
- Live-unverified: Real-Time Mode, transformWithState (row API, MapState TTL), the
  Kafka / Event Hubs / Kinesis connectors, the foreach Postgres sink, the wheel
  artifact on the job cluster, DAB-deployed pipelines referencing a not yet
  uploaded SQL file, Debezium encodings beyond the defaults.
- One stream per deployment at a time (max_concurrent_runs: 1). The slot pipeline
  still reads the CDF while the stream reads the topic (two consumers, reconciled
  by the tick). A deleted slot stays visible through `_sync` until it syncs.
- The bundle now builds the app wheel on every deploy (`uv build`), realtime or not.
- A deployment that turns realtime off stops no stream on later builds (stop it
  with POST /dtwin/incremental/realtime/stop).
- `aws_attributes` in the job cluster are AWS-only; other clouds need a target
