## Fix: Phase 3 review
================================================================================

Context: Review of Phase 3 (realtime): four Critical findings (the stream ran
in a mode Real-Time Mode refuses, batched its upserts, left a frozen `_live` in
the graph, and its slot pipelines could not be adopted by DAB), ten Important
ones (seeding, purge, identities, sizing, runtime, the import closure, cloud
coupling, one stream per domain, poison envelopes, docs) and minors. B's core
files (SlotChange, SlotRowProjector, SlotDiffProcessor, processor.py) are
untouched.

Changes:

1. src/jobs/triple_stream/main.py, LiveSink.py (new) (C1, C2)
   `transformWithState` and the sink run in update output mode, the only one
   Real-Time Mode runs; the real-time trigger and `.start()` sit inside the
   fallback, so a runtime that refuses either falls back to `processingTime`
   with the conf reset. The sink is a `foreach` writer (`LiveSink`) that
   upserts each change as it arrives (`INSERT … VALUES … ON CONFLICT … WHERE
   EXCLUDED.seq > live.seq`, autocommit) instead of staging a batch.
2. src/jobs/triple_stream/TripleStreamEnvelope.py (new), main.py (I9, minors)
   Extract Class: envelope parse / explode moved out of the job. An envelope
   that does not parse, has no seq, names an unmapped table or holds a value
   that does not decode is skipped and counted per reason. A bare Debezium
   table name matches the mapped table of that leaf name when unique. The job
   uses the repo logger and warns that Kinesis is experimental.
3. src/back/core/graphdb/lakebase/_companion_ddl.py, LakebaseLiveTable.py (C3, I1, I3c)
   `_live` is in the union view only while served (table comment
   `ontobricks:live:serving`). `attach` truncates, seeds from the `_slots`
   snapshot (`seed_rows`: blank objects dropped, `SNAPSHOT_SEQ`) and serves;
   `detach` truncates and stops serving. `ensure` grants the stream role USAGE
   on the schema and SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE on `_live`. The purge raises
   `ValidationError` on a bad argument.
4. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/TwinLiveServing.py, TwinRealtimeJob.py (new),
   TwinRealtimeStream.py, __init__.py (C3, I1, I2, I8, minors)
   `start` cancels a run of the same domain at another version, reuses a run of
   this version, else creates, grants, seeds and serves `_live` (warehouse read
   of `_slots`) before `run_now`. `stop` cancels and retires `_live`; a
   non-realtime build on a Lakebase store with a served `_live` does the same.
   `after_tick` retires a served `_live` whose stream no longer runs and
   otherwise purges tombstones older than max(24, TTL) hours. The TTL
   (`state_ttl_hours`, default 72) is a job parameter. `resolve_job_id` tries
   `jobs.list(name=…)` first; `_ACTIVE_STATES` is gone.
5. src/back/objects/registry/schedule/build.py (I2)
   The scheduled tick of a realtime domain on Lakebase calls `after_tick`
   (best-effort) and records its facts.
6. src/back/core/graphdb/RealtimeSource.py, TwinIncrementalReadiness.py,
   domain-information.js (minors)
   `state_ttl_hours` is a validated config field; Kinesis is marked
   experimental; the readiness facts include `backend_eligible` and
   `experimental`.
7. src/back/core/helpers/TripleProjectionSql.py (new), SlotProjectionCompiler.py,
   SparqlTranslator.py, back/core/__init__.py, shared/config/__init__.py,
   back/core/errors/__init__.py, shared/config/constants.py, w3c/owl/* (I6)
   The stream job's import closure is cut loose from the app: the projection
   SQL the translator and the compiler share moved into `TripleProjectionSql`
   (the compiler no longer imports the translator and rdflib); `back.core` and
   `shared.config` re-export nothing (no caller used them); `ErrorResponse`
   (pydantic) is imported from its module by the API layer only;
   `ONTOBRICKS_NS` (rdflib) moved from the shared constants to
   `back.core.w3c.owl.iri`. A subprocess test asserts that `back.core.streaming`
   and the job import no `back.objects`, api, front, agents, fastapi, starlette,
   neo4j, rdflib or pydantic.
8. databricks.yml, pyproject.toml, resources/triple_rtm.job.yml (I6)
   No app wheel: the cluster imports the synced `src` through `PYTHONPATH` and
   installs only `psycopg` and `databricks-sql-connector` (DBR 19 does not ship
   it); the runtime's pyarrow is never pinned. The `ontobricks_wheel` artifact
   and `src/jobs` in the wheel packages are gone.
9. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/TwinRealtimeJob.py, TwinRealtimeStream.py (I3b)
   The mappings go to `<checkpoint root>/_mappings/<run>.json` on the
   checkpoint volume (Files API), which the job's run-as identity (the deployer)
   can read; the checkpoint root must be a `/Volumes/` path.
10. resources/triple_rtm.job.yml, databricks.yml, _ensure-instance-target.sh (C3, I4, I7)
    The task retries three times a minute apart. `spark.sql.shuffle.partitions`
    comes from `var.realtime_shuffle_partitions` (default 4) and Arrow batches
    hold 100 records; two workers by default (task slots >= topic partitions +
    shuffle partitions). The job is cloud-neutral: no `aws_attributes`, no node
    type default; the AWS targets (dev, dev-lakebase, the generated
    dev-lakebase-<id>) set i3.xlarge and on-demand workers.
11. scripts/deploy.sh, scripts/_internal/_select-spark-version.py (new) (I5)
    `deploy.sh` passes the workspace's newest DBR 19 (LTS first, ML / GPU /
    Photon / ARM skipped) as `realtime_spark_version`; a failed lookup keeps the
    bundle default (17.3 LTS, commented to bump to the 19 LTS key).
12. scripts/bootstrap/app-permissions.sh (I3a)
    The job grant is a `_grant_job_run` function, applied to the graph analytics
    job and to the realtime stream job (CAN_MANAGE_RUN for both app principals).
13. scripts/_internal/_render-slot-pipelines.py, SlotPipelineRunner.py,
    scripts/deploy.sh, .gitignore (C4, minor)
    The renderer lists each rendered slot pipeline that exists outside any bundle
    (`SlotPipelineRunner.bundle_managed`) in `_generated_triple_slots.bind`;
    `deploy.sh` binds each (`bundle deployment bind … --auto-approve`) before
    `bundle deploy`, skipping with a notice on a CLI without the subcommand. A
    version whose mappings no longer compile keeps its previous resource
    (logged), so a compile error never plans a deletion. A skipped render
    removes a stale bind list.
14. src/front/routes/domain.py, _domain_information.html (minor)
    The route supplies the realtime source and `RealtimeSource.kind_options`
    (Kinesis labelled experimental); the template keeps no `{% set %}` or
    inline kind list.
15. docs/incremental-materialization.md, README.md (I10)
    Traceability (serving ✅, DAB adoption), the update-mode `foreach` writer and
    why not the native `postgresql` sink (no `seq` guard), seeding / serving /
    retire / purge, updated slots showing old and new until the sync, why the
    slot pipeline reads the CDF and not the topic, the RTM slot rule, Arrow
    batches, the DBR 19 rationale, no wheel, identities and grants, the bind
    step, Kinesis experimental, the TTL default and the live-unverified list.
16. tests
    New closure, runtime picker, bind-list, compile-failure, bundle-managed,
    kind-option, AWS-override, retry and sizing tests; the property test's
    baseline is the seeded `_live`; existing tests follow the moved helpers and
    the volume upload.

