## Realtime: the slot pipeline consumes the topic
================================================================================

Context: Phase 3 design item "the Phase 1 slot pipeline consumes the same topic
to keep Delta in sync". Until now the slot pipeline read the source tables'
change data feed in every mode; a realtime domain's `_slots` / `_data` now
follow the same Debezium topic as the `_live` stream (Implementer B; the build
wiring and docs are Implementer A's).

Changes:

1. src/back/core/streaming/TopicSource.py (new)
   Frozen record of the topic a realtime slot pipeline reads:
   `bootstrap_servers`, `topic`, `secret_scope`, `secret_key`,
   `security_protocol` (`SASL_SSL`), `sasl_mechanism` (`PLAIN`), `kind`
   (`kafka`: the secret holds the SASL JAAS line; `eventhubs`: the namespace
   connection string, `$ConnectionString` login). Every field is validated
   (it is interpolated into SQL); `from_realtime_source()` builds it from a
   domain's `realtime_source` (Kinesis refused: no Kafka endpoint);
   `read_kafka_sql()` emits `STREAM read_kafka(bootstrapServers => …,
   subscribe => …, startingOffsets => 'earliest', kafka.security.protocol =>
   …, kafka.sasl.mechanism => …, kafka.sasl.jaas.config => secret('<scope>',
   '<key>') …)`. Only the secret's names are in the SQL; `secret()` is
   resolved when the pipeline runs, so `SlotPipelineRunner` passes nothing
   through the pipeline configuration.
2. src/back/core/streaming/TopicSlotSource.py (new)
   The topic slot-event view of a row-local mapping: `from_json(CAST(value
   AS STRING), <envelope schema>)` (optionally under `payload`, images as
   lower-cased `MAP<STRING, STRING>`), `source.table` matched by full or —
   when no other mapped table shares it — leaf name, case-insensitively;
   `d` deletes the key of `before`, `c` / `u` / `r` upsert `after`, a `u`
   whose `before` has another key also deletes the old key; objects, NULL
   and blank handling, the subject and the key follow the change-feed view;
   deletes rank 0, upserts 1; the Kafka `offset` is `_commit_version`. The
   view has the change-feed view's columns, so the AUTO CDC flow is reused.
3. src/back/core/streaming/SlotProjectionCompiler.py
   `compile(..., source="cdf" | "topic", topic=None)`: `topic` compiles the
   topic views (a topic is required; a change-feed source takes none; an
   unknown source is a `ValidationError`); the `_slots` DDL and the AUTO CDC
   flows are unchanged.
4. src/back/core/streaming/SlotPipelineSpec.py
   `source` (`"cdf"` | `"topic"`) and `topic` fields; `needs_row_tracking`
   is `False` for a topic source (no row-tracking probe on the sources);
   `source_tables` are still the mapped tables.
5. src/back/core/streaming/__init__.py
   Re-exports `TopicSlotSource` and `TopicSource`.
6. Tests: tests/units/streaming/test_topic_source.py (validation,
   `from_realtime_source`, pinned `read_kafka` SQL, Event Hubs JAAS),
   tests/units/streaming/test_topic_slot_source.py (pinned view SQL,
   composite key, ambiguous leaf, escaping, the change-feed view's columns
   and stack order), tests/units/streaming/test_slot_projection_compiler_topic.py
   (source / topic arguments, unchanged slots DDL and flows, spec fields),
   tests/property/test_slot_topic_property.py (the topic variant's event
   model folds to the same `_slots` as the change-feed variant for the same
   history — payload wrapping, column case, table-name forms and an unmapped
   table's records included — with the model's rules checked against the
   compiled SQL).

