## Fix: the topic slot pipeline parses in SDP and types Debezium values
================================================================================

Context: review of the topic-fed slot pipeline (commits 345ac733, 9840cfbc)
against the Databricks docs. CRITICAL: `read_kafka` requires backticks around
`kafka.`-prefixed consumer options, so every topic view failed to parse.
IMPORTANT: images are read as `MAP<STRING, STRING>`, so stock Debezium's
encodings (epoch-day dates, epoch timestamps, base64 decimals) diverged from
the change feed's `CAST(<column> AS STRING)`; the topic's preconditions were
undocumented; the SQL had never met a real SDP. Plus minors (reserved
identifiers, duplicate-key failure, private cross-class calls, duplicated
patterns, unused options, shared leaf names, leaf case). Implementer B.

Changes:

1. src/back/core/streaming/TopicSource.py
   `read_kafka_sql()` backticks `kafka.security.protocol`,
   `kafka.sasl.mechanism` and `kafka.sasl.jaas.config`. The unused
   `security_protocol` / `sasl_mechanism` options are removed: the login is
   always `SASL_SSL` / `PLAIN`, as in the stream job. Field validation uses
   `RealtimeSource.parse` (one home for the patterns; imported on construction
   only, so the stream job's executors do not load `back.core.graphdb`), plus
   non-empty, unpadded strings. The connection stays in the SQL: a new broker
   list or topic is a new offset space and must replay; a credential is
   rotated under the same secret scope / key, which changes no SQL. The SDP
   docs show `${key}` configuration only inside a WHERE literal and say
   nothing of `read_kafka` options or `secret()` arguments, so the names are
   not moved to the pipeline configuration.
2. src/back/core/streaming/DebeziumValueText.py (new)
   SQL turning a Debezium value's JSON text into the text of its typed
   column, with the stream job's `SparkColumnText` rules: epoch days for a
   DATE; epoch milli / micro / nanoseconds (by magnitude) for a TIMESTAMP;
   numeric text or the base64 two's-complement unscaled bytes for a DECIMAL
   (byte fold with `try_add` / `try_multiply`, then `E-<scale>`); true words or
   non-zero numbers for a BOOLEAN; `try_cast` for integral and floating types;
   base64 for BINARY; other types keep the text. Residuals named in the module
   docstring: from_json cannot tell a numeric string from a number (digit
   strings in a date / timestamp / boolean column); the timestamp unit guess
   misreads micro / nanoseconds within about 3 years of 1970 (shared with the
   stream job); HALF_UP rounding for excess fraction digits; nested types keep
   JSON text; the session time zone (UTC by default); an unreadable value is
   NULL here where the stream job skips the record.
3. src/back/core/streaming/TopicSlotSource.py
   `slot_event_view_sql(..., match_leaf=False, types=None)`: the full table
   name matches by default; `types` (`{column: UC type}`) converts the
   mapping's typed columns once per image (`transform_values`). `offset` and
   `table` are backticked (reserved under `enforceReservedKeywords`). Image
   columns are lower-cased without `DUPLICATED_MAP_KEY`: of two columns
   differing only in case the last one wins, as in the stream job (whose rows
   are Python dicts). New `view_emitter(mappings, *, topic, column_types)`
   (moved from the compiler): validates the topic, lower-cases tables
   consistently, decides `match_leaf`, and warns once per table about mapped
   columns without a type and about a leaf name shared by two mapped tables
   (never matched by stock Debezium's bare names). The module docstring
   states the topic preconditions: keyed by the source row's primary key,
   full pre-images (`REPLICA IDENTITY FULL` / `binlog_row_image=FULL`), and
   retention / compaction for a full refresh's replay from `earliest`
   (neither the mappings nor the realtime config can tell, so not checked).
4. src/back/core/streaming/SlotProjectionCompiler.py
   `compile(..., column_types=None)` passes the types to the topic views (the
   change feed reads typed columns and ignores them). `require_ident` /
   `require_fqn` are public (no private cross-class calls); the topic branch
   of `_view_emitter` moved to `TopicSlotSource.view_emitter`; `compile()`
   reuses `row_local_mappings` instead of repeating its loop (492 -> 480 lines).
5. src/back/core/streaming/__init__.py
   Re-exports `DebeziumValueText`.
6. Tests: tests/units/streaming/test_topic_source.py (backticked options,
   fixed login, RealtimeSource rules), tests/units/streaming/test_topic_slot_source.py
   (re-pinned view SQL, typed values, case-duplicate columns, emitter and its
   warnings), tests/units/streaming/test_debezium_value_text.py (new, pinned
   conversions), tests/units/streaming/test_slot_projection_compiler_topic.py
   (`column_types`), tests/property/test_debezium_value_property.py (new: the
   SQL rule's model equals `SparkColumnText` for generated dates, timestamps,
   decimals and booleans; mutants of the sign rule and the nanosecond floor
   are caught), tests/property/test_slot_topic_property.py (case-duplicate
   columns, re-pinned fragments), tests/external/test_topic_pipeline_sql.py
   (new, `external`: a development pipeline with the compiled topic SQL runs a
   validate-only update, then is deleted; skipped without
   `ONTOBRICKS_EXTERNAL_PIPELINE=1`, `ONTOBRICKS_EXTERNAL_SCHEMA` and
   credentials).
7. Verified outside the suite on local Spark 4.0.1 (ANSI and
   `enforceReservedKeywords` on; `read_kafka` and the change feed replaced by
   local tables): the converter SQL equals `SparkColumnText` on 12,027
   Debezium-encoded values (the only mismatches are the shared timestamp-unit
   window); the compiled topic view and the change-feed view emit identical
   slot events for 400 typed inserts, and fold to identical `_slots` (567
   slots) over 592 inserts, updates, re-keys and deletes.

