## `_graph` MV, Neo4j net apply, topic-fed realtime pipeline, freshness harness
================================================================================

Context: round A2 of incremental triple materialization closes four design items
that were still deviations or deferred: `_graph` as a materialized view
Lakehouse//RT can read (Phase 1 P0), net changes for Neo4j (Phase 1 P1), the
realtime slot pipeline consuming the Debezium topic (Phase 3; Implementer B's
compiler, wired here), and the freshness / drift KPIs (design "measure"
section). It continues a stopped implementer's uncommitted `_graph` work.

Changes:

1. src/back/core/graphdb/delta/GraphRelation.py (new),
   src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/TwinGraphRelation.py (new)
   `GraphRelation`: `…_graph` as the union VIEW or a materialized view
   (`ensure_materialized` drops the VIEW first, `replace_with_view` the MV,
   `refresh` / `refresh_materialized`), and `refresh_after_write(client,
   written_fqn)`: the one hook every `…_inferred` writer calls (`REFRESH …
   ASYNC` when `…_graph` is an MV, nothing for a VIEW or another table,
   never raises). `TwinGraphRelation`: an incremental / microbatch build on
   the Lakehouse engine makes `…_graph` an MV (`REFRESH POLICY INCREMENTAL`,
   row tracking on `…_inferred`, its own fingerprint, `TRIGGER ON UPDATE`
   when `…_data` refreshes itself), keeps it while its definition holds and
   refreshes it right after `…_data`; Lakebase / Neo4j (whose readers use
   their store; `realtime` is Lakebase-only) keep the VIEW and replace a
   leftover MV. `graph_relation` (`mv` / `view`) is in the build-run trace.
2. src/back/core/graphdb/delta/MaterializedViewBuilder.py
   `graph_mv_sql` carries the definition fingerprint and an optional refresh
   clause (`graph_mv_sha`); `refresh_sql(..., wait=False)` adds `ASYNC`;
   `apply(..., graph_refresh_clause=)`.
3. src/back/core/graphdb/delta/DeltaFlatStore.py,
   src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/TwinBuildPostMaterialize.py,
   src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/TwinScheduledRefresh.py,
   src/back/core/graphdb/delta/DeltaTripleStoreBuildPipeline.py,
   src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/TwinIncrementalBuild.py,
   src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/TwinBuildRunHistory.py,
   src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/_build_pipeline.py
   Store inserts (reasoning, cohorts, raw `materialize_to_delta` into a
   companion) and the inferred purge refresh a graph MV; the build's
   inferred reset refreshes it synchronously instead of recreating the VIEW;
   the scheduled tick refreshes it after the in-place `…_data` refresh; the
   standalone Delta build (CTAS `…_data`) and the full path replace it by the
   VIEW.
4. src/back/core/graphdb/delta/InferredTripleLedger.py (new),
   src/back/core/graphdb/GraphDBFactory.py, src/back/core/graphdb/neo4j/Neo4jStore.py,
   src/back/core/reasoning/ReasoningService.py, src/back/core/graph_analysis/CohortBuilder.py
   A Neo4j store gets an `InferredTripleLedger` (domains that are not
   `full`): reasoning and cohort writers list every batch in the Delta
   `…_inferred` table before writing it to Neo4j (a failed listing writes
   nothing).
5. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/TwinNetChangeApply.py
   For a store with a ledger the purge runs before the net changes: every
   listed triple `…_data` does not assert (`<inferred> EXCEPT <data>`,
   streamed through `iter_rows` into `delete_triples` in batches of 500) is
   deleted, the `…_data` triples on the same subject and predicate are
   written again (Neo4j keeps one value per property, label set and name),
   and the list is emptied. Neo4j leaves the full stream;
   `inferred_not_separable` stays for a store with neither purge path; an
   unreadable list falls back as `inferred_unreadable`.
6. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/TwinIncrementalBuild.py,
   src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/TwinIncrementalReadiness.py,
   src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/TwinScheduledRefresh.py,
   src/back/objects/registry/schedule/build.py,
   src/front/static/domain/js/domain-information.js
   `compile_for` picks the slot source once for the build, the tick, the MERGE
   fingerprint, the preflight and the DAB renderer: `source="topic"` with
   `TopicSource.from_realtime_source(...)` when the domain's best mode is
   `realtime` (`slot_topic`; Kinesis keeps the change feed), and the source
   tables' `column_types` from `DESCRIBE TABLE` (once per compile, on the
   build's or tick's warehouse; an undescribable source is an
   `InfrastructureError`, not other SQL). `feed_tables(spec)` is empty for a
   topic-fed pipeline, so the build, the tick and the preflight probe no row
   tracking and the slot refresh plan reads no source history; the preflight
   reports `row_tracking_required: false` with the sources unprobed, which
   the domain panel no longer flags. The MERGE fallback needs no change: it
   never applies to a `realtime` request (pinned by a test).
7. scripts/measure_freshness.py (new), tests/external/test_freshness_slo.py (new),
   .github/workflows/nightly.yml
   `FreshnessProbe` updates one source row N times (default 5, spaced) and
   times each change until it is visible in `…_data` / `…_graph` (warehouse,
   optionally the Lakehouse//RT one) and the Lakebase synced table / `_live`;
   p50 / p95 / p99 per path, reconciliation with the batch recompute, the
   synced table and `_live`, the row restored, the mode's SLOs checked
   (`microbatch` `_graph` <= 30 s p95 and Lakebase <= 60 s p95, `realtime`
   `_live` <= 1 s p99, no drift). The external test asserts them for a
   configured domain; the nightly `external-smoke` job runs it as a
   non-blocking step with a step summary (timeout 25 minutes).
8. docs/incremental-materialization.md, README.md
   Modes table (`_graph` column), "The `_graph` relation", Lakehouse//RT,
   net-change apply (the Neo4j EXCEPT rule), the realtime slot pipeline on
   the topic with its preconditions, Verification (the harness), Design
   traceability (`_data` / `_graph` MVs and the P1 net changes ✅, the KPI
   row), Known limitations.

Deviations:
- `_graph` is a materialized view on the Lakehouse engine only: Lakebase and
  Neo4j domains (and so every `realtime` domain) keep the union VIEW, which no
  reader of theirs queries; an MV there would copy `…_data` for nothing.
- The Neo4j purge also rewrites the asserted triples a deleted listed literal
  unset (not in the brief; needed for equality with a full stream).
- The freshness harness has not been run against a workspace yet.

