## Fix: round A2 review
================================================================================

Context: the review of round A2 (`_graph` MV, Neo4j net apply, topic-fed
realtime pipeline, freshness harness) found no Critical and five Important
findings (I1-I4 fixed here; the fifth is the rules item, minor 11), plus
eleven minors.

Changes:

1. src/back/core/graphdb/delta/GraphRelation.py, MaterializedViewBuilder.py,
   src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/TwinGraphRelation.py, TwinBuildPostMaterialize.py
   I1: `refresh_after_write` refreshes a `_graph` MV synchronously (the
   ASYNC variant is gone), so the graph caches the writers rebuild next
   (reasoning, cohorts, the purge) read the new union and back-to-back
   writes are never left to a later refresh; errors stay best-effort. A
   build refreshes the MV once, in the inferred reset (minor 8). Docstrings:
   realtime keeps the VIEW; a failed kind probe reads as a VIEW (minor 7).
2. src/back/objects/registry/schedule/build.py
   I2: a scheduled tick on the Lakehouse engine no longer drops / creates an
   unqualified `<Name>_V<n>` table nor appends the asserted graph to
   `_inferred`: like the main build's `skips_graph_stream` it decides the
   mode, refreshes `_data` in place (or builds it from the gateway VIEW as a
   table or the pass-through view), refreshes a `_graph` MV and returns the
   `_data` count. The `_slot_spec` docstring states that a failed DESCRIBE
   fails the tick on purpose (minor 4).
3. scripts/measure_freshness.py, .github/workflows/nightly.yml
   I3: the reconciliation runs once the last change is seen and before the
   row is restored. I4: each path is polled on its own thread (one Postgres
   connection per Lakebase path), timed from the write; `realtime` polls
   `live` by default and a Lakebase path without its DSN and table fails
   fast. Minor 9: a key naming no row and a table outside `--allow-pattern`
   (default `*ob_it_*,*fixture*`) are usage errors with nothing written;
   numeric value columns get numeric markers written through CAST; an empty
   variable reads as unset; the nightly step documents
