## Microbatch Lakehouse//RT fast path: reads `_slots` ∪ `_inferred` directly
================================================================================

Context: the design has the Delta engine on a Lakehouse//RT warehouse read
`_graph` / `_slots` directly so that `microbatch` freshness equals the slot
pipeline's commit cadence. Every Lakehouse read went to `_graph`, the
`TRIGGER ON UPDATE` materialized view chained after `_data`, measured live at
217–383 s behind the pipeline. A `microbatch` domain without batch mappings now
reads the slots inline when it is read through Lakehouse//RT.

Changes:

1. src/back/core/graphdb/delta/GraphReadRelation.py (new), src/back/core/graphdb/delta/__init__.py
   `GraphReadRelation` decides a domain's read relation: `slots_live` only when
   the domain is on the Lakehouse engine, "Use Lakehouse//RT for queries" is on
   (`resolve_lakehouse_use_sea`), its last successful build (scheduled ticks and
   failures passed over; the requested mode without one) ran `microbatch` with
   a `slots_table` and `batch_mappings == 0`, `_slots` exists and `_data` still
   is the materialized view (`information_schema.tables`, build warehouse);
   anything else, or any failing lookup, is `graph`. A `full` / `incremental`
   request or another engine is answered without any read. Decisions are cached
   per slots table (one per domain version) for 30 s (`TTL_S`). The inline
   relation is `(SELECT subject, predicate, object FROM <slots> WHERE object IS
   NOT NULL AND TRIM(object) != '' UNION SELECT subject, predicate, object FROM
   <inferred>)` (`NON_BLANK_OBJECT_SQL`; `SELECT DISTINCT` over the slots alone
   for asserted-only reads), built only from names that pass `SAFE_SQL_IDENT`;
   `physical` maps it back to `_graph` / `_data`. Re-exported from the package.
2. src/back/core/helpers/SQLHelpers.py
   `effective_graph_query_table` returns the inline relation for `slots_live`
   (Lakehouse engine) and takes `physical=True` for callers that need the
   table name.
3. src/back/core/graphdb/delta/DeltaFlatStore.py, src/back/core/graphdb/entity_search.py
   `_sql_relation` passes an inline relation through (reads render
   `FROM (…)` and alias it as their templates do, `FROM (…) t`); a cache
   rebuild maps it back to `_graph` (`rebuild_adjacency`);
   `is_asserted_only_relation` recognises the slots-only relation. The RT
   guardrail fallback retries the same inline SQL on the build warehouse;
   `last_read_route` is unchanged. Class at 791 LOC.
4. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/cache/TwinStoreCache.py, src/api/routers/digitaltwin.py,
   src/api/routers/internal/dtwin.py, src/back/objects/digitaltwin/TwinGraphAccess.py
   Status probes (`table_exists` / `get_status`), existence checks, display
   names and the analytics run's graph name ask for the physical name
   (`physical=True`, forwarded by `TwinGraphAccess.graph_query_table` and the
   route wrapper); read routes keep the default.
5. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/node/NodeContextService.py
   A bridge target's relation is accepted when it is a plain FQN or the inline
   relation (`_readable_relation`; the baselined `_resolve_bridges` did not grow).
6. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/TwinIncrementalBuild.py, TwinBuildRunHistory.py
   A build records `batch_mappings` (the spec's batch mapping count; `None`
   when no incremental build ran or it fell back) in
   `stats.materialization`; `TwinBuildRunHistory.last_success_facts` reads the
   newest successful main build's facts.
7. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/TwinIncrementalStatus.py, TwinIncrementalReadiness.py
   Both reports carry `read_relation` (`graph` | `slots_live`); a `full`
   domain's status still makes no warehouse, pipelines or registry call.
8. tests/units/graphdb/delta/test_graph_read_relation.py (new) — decision
   matrix (RT off, incremental, full, other engine, ran-as-incremental, batch
   mappings, missing fact, no slots, no build, missing slots table, `_data` no
   longer the view, failing read, default build-warehouse probe), TTL reuse /
   expiry / per-version key, pinned SQL of both relations, `physical`,
   unsafe names, `effective_graph_query_table` for both outcomes and
   `physical`, DeltaFlatStore reads (`FROM (…) WHERE`, aliased `FROM (…) t`),
   the RT fallback with the subquery, the cache rebuild on `_graph`, the
