## Fix: fast-path review
================================================================================

Context: the review of the microbatch Lakehouse//RT fast path (`bf217fbc`)
requested changes (2 P1, 10 P2). The fast path is re-founded on `_data`'s stored
definition fingerprint and moved inside `DeltaFlatStore`, so
`effective_graph_query_table` is a pure name lookup again.

Changes:

1. src/back/core/graphdb/delta/GraphReadRelation.py
   The decision no longer reads build history (it used to skip a newer failed or
   cancelled build that had already replaced `_data` with a batch-branch view, and
   could drop the batch triples). `slots_live` iff the domain is on the Lakehouse
   engine, requested a continuous mode (no read otherwise), has "Use
   Lakehouse//RT for queries" on (no probe otherwise) and `_data`'s
   `ontobricks.mv_sql_sha256` equals `data_mv_sha(slots, no batch branch,
   TRIGGER ON UPDATE)` — one `SHOW TBLPROPERTIES` saying `_data` is the
   microbatch view over the non-blank slots alone (the incremental view, with no
   refresh clause, has another fingerprint; a CTAS table has none). The probe
   runs on the reading store's client (the reader's identity, in the worker
   thread the read already runs in; no build-warehouse client, no `back/objects`
   import). An absent `_data` reads as `graph` quietly, any other failing probe
   logs a warning (once per TTL). Cache key: the `_data` FQN, 30 s TTL. New
   `for_read(table_name, domain, settings, client)` swaps this domain's `_graph`
   FQN for `(SELECT DISTINCT … FROM <slots> WHERE <non-blank> UNION ALL SELECT …
   FROM <inferred>)` — `_graph`'s multiset exactly — and its `_data` FQN for the
   distinct non-blank slots; both strings are built explicitly
   (`relation_sql`, `asserted_relation_sql`). `physical`, `is_inline`,
   `includes_inferred` and `read_relation` are gone.
2. src/back/core/graphdb/delta/MaterializedViewBuilder.py
   `existing_mv_sha(..., strict=True)` raises a failed lookup (an absent
   relation still reads as `""`).
3. src/back/core/graphdb/delta/DeltaFlatStore.py
   `_sql_relation` (hence `sql_table_reference`) returns `GraphReadRelation.for_read`
   for an FQN; logical names still resolve to the views. `query_triples` /
   `count_triples` read through `_sql_relation` and `execute_query(…,
   bounded=False)`: they gain the RT guardrail fallback and keep running without
   the statement timeout (full-graph dumps may legitimately run long).
   `rebuild_adjacency` no longer maps back (a rebuild reads the same relation as
   the reads). Class at 789 LOC.
4. src/back/core/helpers/SQLHelpers.py, src/back/objects/digitaltwin/TwinGraphAccess.py,
   src/back/objects/digitaltwin/cache/TwinStoreCache.py, src/api/routers/internal/dtwin.py,
   src/back/core/graphdb/entity_search.py
   Reverted to their pre-fast-path state: no `physical` parameter or sites, no
   inline sniffing in `is_asserted_only_relation`.
5. src/api/routers/digitaltwin.py, src/back/objects/digitaltwin/node/NodeContextService.py
   The `dt_triples` type filter and the bridge `seed_where` build their subquery
   over `store.sql_table_reference(table)`; the bridge's strict `SAFE_SQL_IDENT`
   guard is restored (`_readable_relation` removed).
6. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/TwinIncrementalBuild.py
   `GraphReadRelation.clear_cache()` (this process only) in `_leave` (so also on
   `_fall_back`) and in `_apply_views` once `_data` has its definition.
7. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/TwinBuildRunHistory.py
   `last_success_facts` deleted; the `batch_mappings` trace fact stays.
8. Tests — tests/units/graphdb/delta/test_graph_read_relation.py rewritten:
