## Live Lakehouse//RT verification of the microbatch fast path (fevm-ontobricks-int)
================================================================================

Context: the user created a Lakehouse//RT warehouse ("realtime", serverless,
Large; the API lists it with `warehouse_type: null`) on the integration
workspace, which unblocked the one KPI the design asks for that had no live
evidence. The fast path was exercised end to end on fixture tables in a
scratch schema (dropped afterwards), with reads going through the app's own
`DatabricksClient(use_sea=True)` (Statement Execution API) on that warehouse
and DDL / mutations on the build warehouse.

Observed (2026-11-02):
- The fingerprint probe (`SHOW TBLPROPERTIES` on `_data`) runs on the RT
  warehouse and matches `GraphReadRelation.microbatch_data_sha`.
- Every read shape the store emits ran on RT over the inline relation
  (`SELECT DISTINCT … FROM _slots … UNION ALL SELECT … FROM _inferred`):
  unaliased `FROM (…)`, `FROM (…) t`, a self join, the asserted-only form, the
  `subject IN (SELECT …)` seed, and direct reads of the streaming table and
  the MV. The inferred triple is visible through the relation and its count
  equals `_data` + `_inferred`.
- Lakehouse//RT refuses recursive CTEs (`[UNSUPPORTED_FEATURE] Recursive CTEs
  is not supported in Lakehouse//RT … SQLSTATE: 0A000`), so the BFS /
  transitive-closure templates cannot run there. The message carries the
  `lakehouse//rt` fallback marker, so `DeltaFlatStore.execute_query` retries
  those on the build warehouse (`last_read_route = build-fallback`); pinned by
  a new unit test with the verbatim message.
- Point reads of the relation from a laptop through the SEA: p50 216 ms,
  p95 404 ms, max 541 ms (n = 20; includes the HTTP round trip).
- Freshness, continuous slot pipeline, source commit → visible through the RT
  relation: samples 22.9, 9.8, 15.8, 14.6, 16.2, 13.5, 15.2, 10.4, 9.5, 10.7 s
  (n = 10) — p50 14.0 s, p95 22.9 s, max 22.9 s. The design's `microbatch`
  KPI (≤ 30 s p95 through Lakehouse//RT) is met.

