## Snapshot fallback when an MV-sourced Lakebase sync hits the change-feed preview wall
================================================================================

Context: measured live, a triggered or continuous synced table on the `_data`
materialized view creates and snapshots, then its sync pipeline fails with
`MATERIALIZED_VIEW_CDF_REQUIRES_EXTERNAL_METADATA` (the MV change-feed private
preview). A build whose slots do not carry the whole graph (batch mappings)
still has to sync `_data`; it must not fail the build or leave the registration
in `SYNCED_TABLE_ONLINE_PIPELINE_FAILED`.

Changes:

1. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/TwinLakebaseSync.py —
   `trigger_and_wait(mgr, synced_uc, plan, *, timeout_s, data_is_mv, …)`
   returns `(state, plan synced)`: a triggered / continuous `triples` plan on a
   materialized view whose wait fails with `PIPELINE_FAILED` is re-registered
   as a snapshot of the same relation (`ensure` recreates a registration whose
   policy changed; the union-view dropper runs before the delete) and synced
   again; a cancellation, any other failure, and a failed snapshot propagate.
   `sync_and_wait(pipe, …)` is the build's wrapper: it records
   `sync_mode_effective = snapshot` and `sync_fallback_reason =
   mv_change_feed_unavailable` (`MV_CHANGE_FEED_UNAVAILABLE`) on the pipe.
2. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/_build_pipeline.py — step 5 of the
   managed-sync apply calls `TwinLakebaseSync.sync_and_wait` (the
   `_apply_via_synced_pipeline` function shrank by three lines);
   `sync_fallback_reason` attribute.
3. src/back/objects/registry/schedule/build.py — the tick's wait goes through
   `TwinLakebaseSync.trigger_and_wait` with `data_is_mv` = the view was kept.
4. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/TwinBuildPostMaterialize.py — trace fact
   `sync_fallback_reason` (the status endpoint's `last_build.materialization`
   carries it with the other facts).
5. src/front/static/global/js/runs-render.js — run details show "Sync Source
   Kind" and "Sync Fallback" when recorded.
6. docs/incremental-materialization.md — per-backend Lakebase paragraph (source
   rule, asserted view, fallback, resync cost, live status name), Scheduled
   builds (the tick's source rule and fallback), Build-run trace rows,
   Reconciliation (`sync_data` counts the asserted view), Preview enrolment
   (MV → Lakebase sync is the same preview; what happens without it),
   Upgrading (one build creates the asserted view).
7. Tests — `TestMVSyncFallback` (re-register + resync, facts recorded, no
   fallback on success, propagation for a table source / an already-snapshot
   plan / a slots source / a non-pipeline failure / a cancellation / a failed
   snapshot); the tick falls back to a snapshot of the kept view; trace key
