## Live: MERGE fallback, source-overwrite detection, row-tracking probe (fevm-ontobricks-int)
================================================================================

Context: three Phase 1 / Phase 2 rows had unit tests only. A warehouse-only
spike on fixture tables (scratch schema, dropped afterwards) exercised the
real code paths; no code change.

Observed (2026-11-02):
- `DeltaMergeMaterializer.apply` (the incremental-without-serverless path):
  the first build creates `_data` with row tracking, deletion vectors and the
  change feed on and merges 3 rows; a build with no source change merges
  **0 rows** (`numOutputRows 0` — cost proportional to change); one changed
  source row → 1 delete + 1 insert (set semantics: the triple's identity
  changed); one deleted source row → 1 delete, 2 rows left. `table_changes`
  on the MERGE table at that version lists exactly the one delete — the
  change feed the net-change apply reads when `_data` is a table works
  without any preview.
- `SourceReadiness.source_overwritten_since`: a plain `UPDATE` is not a
  rewrite; `INSERT OVERWRITE` (`WRITE`, mode Overwrite) and
  `CREATE OR REPLACE TABLE AS SELECT` are detected.
- `SourceReadiness.check`: the table replaced by `CREATE OR REPLACE TABLE AS
  SELECT` lost its properties and reads `row_tracking = false` — exactly what
  the readiness preflight reports and what degrades the mode to `full`.

